{"entryId":"1515","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1515:1","sourceSha256":"8814f72a2cc08750540aa8a9d7e0741e401069ff9ec1545707f6ab89b99c6d12","englishSha256":"da8bdf53332496c60a37af419d790be1d2596c41451045150be558be70c516c9","citations":[{"id":"1515:1:citation-01","he":[0,37],"en":[28,41],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_11b.8"},"reference":"Sanhedrin 11b:8","assessment":"The Sanhedrin witness names Chananyah of Ono.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 11b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_11b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1515:1:citation-02","he":[62,125],"en":[43,73],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_66b.2"},"reference":"Gittin 66b:2","assessment":"Gittin reads Chanina of Ono, and Rashi identifies the imprisoned transmitter as Akiva.","evidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 66b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_66b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Gittin 66b:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Gittin_66b.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1515:1:citation-03","he":[62,125],"en":[165,183],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Gittin_66b.2.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Gittin 66b:2:1","assessment":"Gittin reads Chanina of Ono, and Rashi identifies the imprisoned transmitter as Akiva.","evidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 66b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_66b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Gittin 66b:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Gittin_66b.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[{"raw":"והוא מה' הדנין לפני חכמים (ע\"ש)","reason":"The nearby Bavli named list gives Chakhinai. Rambam separately names Ono and Chakhinai. The identity claim stays qualified.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 17b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_17b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Heilprin says he disagrees with both sages. In the directly quoted instruction to give a get, the prison tradition agrees with Meir about having others write, while Yosi requires the appointees to learn and write it themselves. Rashi names Akiva as the prisoner.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 11b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_11b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 66b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_66b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Gittin 66b:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Gittin_66b.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 17b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_17b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 66b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_66b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 66b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_66b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
